WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:04.164
Make flashcards, quizzes and worksheets that actually stick.

2
00:00:05.664 --> 00:00:10.051
Why spaced repetition and self testing beat rereading, how to turn notes

3
00:00:10.051 --> 00:00:14.560
into cards and quizzes, and the printables that save a teacher an evening.

4
00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:20.215
Why testing beats rereading. When you try to recall an answer, your brain

5
00:00:20.215 --> 00:00:24.237
has to rebuild it, and that effort is what makes the memory stronger.

6
00:00:25.537 --> 00:00:29.908
Quizzes written in plain text. Quiz Maker lets you write a quiz the way

7
00:00:29.908 --> 00:00:34.525
you would type it in a notes app: a question, then the options, with a star

8
00:00:34.525 --> 00:00:35.756
on the right answer.

9
00:00:37.056 --> 00:00:39.963
Grades, GPA and the final exam question.

10
00:00:39.963 --> 00:00:45.123
The question every student asks before a final is simple: what score do

11
00:00:45.123 --> 00:00:45.632
I need?

12
00:00:46.932 --> 00:00:50.943
Private by design. Study notes, class lists and grades are personal.

13
00:00:52.243 --> 00:00:55.256
To try it, open Flashcard Maker in OpenFile.

14
00:00:55.256 --> 00:00:59.160
Drop in a file, adjust the settings and press the button.

15
00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:02.653
It all runs on your device, so nothing is uploaded.

16
00:01:05.343 --> 00:01:08.948
Read the full post, with live demos, on the OpenFile blog.
